§ `Regulation 17.1(14) to (18) - boundaries, ending and notice`

-- src:330 | (14) Where a claimant referred to in subsection (2),(4),(6), (8), (10) or (12) ordinarily resides so near to the boundaries of more than one region that it cannot be determined with certainty in which region the claimant resides, the regional rate of unemployment that applies to that claimant is the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 17.1(14) (src:330)
-- Plain gloss: a claimant under (2), (4), (6), (8), (10) or (12) who lives so near the boundaries of more than one region that the region
-- cannot be determined with certainty takes the highest of the rates that apply for each of those regions. The rates given are those
-- that apply in respect of each region under this regulation or under reg 17(1.1).
GIVEN `the regional rates of unemployment that apply in respect of each of those regions` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 17.1(14) the highest of the regional rates for a claimant who resides near the boundaries of more than one region` IS
    `reg 17(2) and (3) the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions` `the regional rates of unemployment that apply in respect of each of those regions`

-- src:331 | (15) Where a claimant referred to in subsection (3),(5),(7), (9), (11) or (13) was last employed in insurable employment in Canada so near to the boundaries of more than one region that it cannot be determined with certainty in which region the claimant was employed, the regional rate of unemployment that applies to that claimant is the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 17.1(15) (src:331)
-- Plain gloss: the same for a claimant under (3), (5), (7), (9), (11) or (13) who was last employed in insurable employment in Canada so
-- near the boundaries of more than one region that the region cannot be determined with certainty.
GIVEN `the regional rates of unemployment that apply in respect of each of those regions` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 17.1(15) the highest of the regional rates for a claimant last employed near the boundaries of more than one region` IS
    `reg 17(2) and (3) the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions` `the regional rates of unemployment that apply in respect of each of those regions`

-- src:334 | (18) As soon as possible after the condition referred to in subsection (16) or (17) is satisfied, the Commission must publish a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the provisions that cease to have effect. The Commission must also publish the notice on its website.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 17.1(18) (src:334)
-- Plain gloss: when the condition of (16) or (17) is satisfied, the Commission must as soon as possible publish in the Canada Gazette a
-- notice naming the provisions that cease to have effect, and publish it on its website too. This is the Commission's duty; the answer is
-- whether it has been met, and it is met where the duty has not arisen. Whether the notice was published "as soon as possible" is a
-- judgment the caller states. The cessation of (6), (7), (12) and (13) does not wait for the notice (reg 17.1(16), (17)).
GIVEN `the condition referred to in subsection (16) or (17) is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has published a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the provisions that cease to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has also published the notice on its website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was published as soon as possible after the condition was satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 17.1(18) the Commission has published the notice as required` IF
        NOT (`the condition referred to in subsection (16) or (17) is satisfied`)
    OR  (   `the Commission has published a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the provisions that cease to have effect`
        AND `the Commission has also published the notice on its website`
        AND `the notice was published as soon as possible after the condition was satisfied`)

