@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 17 and reg 17.1 (src:242) (src:258)
-- Plain gloss: at most one of reg 17.1(2) to (13) applies to a claimant (one region, resident in Canada or not, one period). The first
-- answer in the list is the one that applies; with none, the claimant's rate is the one reg 17(1.1) to (3) gives.
GIVEN `the answers under reg 17.1(2) to (13) that could apply to the claimant` IS A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 17.1 the first answer that applies` IS
    CONSIDER `the answers under reg 17.1(2) to (13) that could apply to the claimant`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER first
        WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST rate
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `reg 17.1 the first answer that applies` rest

-- src:242 | 17 (1) The regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant is
-- src:258 | (2) For the purposes of sections 7, 7.1, 12 and 14 and Part VIII of the Act, in respect of the period beginning on September 17, 2000 and ending on October 6, 2001, and in the case of a claimant who, during the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act, was ordinarily resident in Madawaska — Charlotte, the applicable regional rate of unemployment is the greater of
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 17 and reg 17.1 (src:242) (src:258)
-- Plain gloss: where reg 17.1 gives "the applicable regional rate of unemployment", that rate is the claimant's; otherwise the rate of reg 17(1.1) to (3).
GIVEN `the answer under reg 17.1` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the answer under reg 17(1.1) to (3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 17 and reg 17.1 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` IS
