    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the answer under reg 17(1.1) to (3)`

§ `Regulation 18 - regions`

-- src:337 | 18 (1) The regions described in Schedule I are hereby established for the purposes of Parts I and VIII of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 18(1) (src:337)
-- Plain gloss: the regions Schedule I (piece er6) describes are the regions for Parts I and VIII of the Act.
GIVEN `the region is described in Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 18(1) the region is established for the purposes of Parts I and VIII of the Act` IF
    `the region is described in Schedule I`

-- src:338 | (2) The Commission shall, at least once every five years after the coming into force of subsection (1), review the boundaries of the regions established by that subsection for the purpose of determining if it is appropriate to make changes to those boundaries.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 18(2) (src:338)
-- Plain gloss: the Commission must review the regions' boundaries at least every five years after subsection (1) came into force. The
-- answer is whether, on the day in question, a review is not yet overdue: the day must be no later than five years after the last review (or
-- after the day subsection (1) came into force, which is in Part VII of the Regulations, piece er6, if there has been none). The review is
-- the Commission's duty; the text states no consequence for the person.
GIVEN `the day of the most recent review of the boundaries, or the day subsection (1) came into force if there has been none` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 18(2) the Commission's review of the boundaries is not overdue` IF
    `the day in question` AT MOST `add years` `the day of the most recent review of the boundaries, or the day subsection (1) came into force if there has been none` 5
